// 186 — W6 inbound TLS: an in-process HTTPS request/response. A server coroutine terminates a
// server-side TLS handshake over an accepted socket (exactly what App does when useTls is set), reads
// an HTTP request over the encrypted TlsStream, and writes an HTTP response; a client coroutine
// TLS-connects and checks the response body. This proves HTTP framing works over TLS through the
// `AsyncIO.recvInto(buf: long, ...)` seam (widened from int so a 64-bit heap buffer address is not
// truncated). Deterministic + self-contained (loopback, embedded self-signed cert). ASAN-clean.
import assert;
import bytes;
import string;
import net.asyncio;
import net.asynctls;

